:"A minimal drop zone. The `onDrop` callback receives the dropped items; use the exported `isFileDropItem` guard to narrow them to files. Wrap the instructional text in `<Text slot=\"label\">` so it labels the visually hidden drop button for screen readers."},"598":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-15","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#disabled","content":"Set `isDisabled` to prevent the drop zone from accepting interactions. The zone is dimmed and the cursor indicates it is not interactive."},"599":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-16","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#file-upload","content":"A reference composition combining `DropZone` with `FileTrigger` to support both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. Use this as a starting point and adapt the accepted formats, size limit, and handlers to your product's requirements."},"600":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-17","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#drop-target-label","content":"Pass a render-prop function as `children` to change the zone's content while a valid drag is active. Branching on `isDropTarget` requires no extra state. Pair it with `getDropOperation` to reject unsupported types - the label only appears when the drag is accepted."},"601":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-18","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#replace-existing-file","content":"Use `children` as a render function to show different content based on the current zone state - here, swapping the default label for \"Drop to replace\" when a file is already selected and a new drag is active. The same `onDrop` handler services both the drag path and the `FileTrigger` click path, so either gesture replaces the selection."},"602":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-19","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Key"},"603":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-20","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Description"},"604":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-21","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"605":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-22","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the drop zone"},"606":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-23","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"`Enter` / `Space`"},"607":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-24","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#keyboard","content":"Opens the file picker so files can be selected without a pointer"},"608":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-25","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The drop zone renders a visually hidden `<button>` inside the container. Assistive technology discovers and announces this button as an interactive element — activating it opens the native file picker without a pointer."},"609":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-26","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"The button's accessible name is built from two sources, combined in order:"},"610":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-27","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`<Text slot=\"label\">`** — any `Text` child with `slot=\"label\"` has its `id` linked to the button via `aria-labelledby`. This is the recommended way to provide a contextual label that is also visible to sighted users."},"611":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-28","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#screen-readers","content":"**`aria-label`** — pass `aria-label` on the `DropZone` component to override or supplement the label (e.g. `aria-label=\"Upload profile photo\"`). When no `Text slot=\"label\"` is present and no `aria-label` is set, the button falls back to the default \"DropZone\" label provided by React Aria."},"612":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-29","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Use the drop zone alongside a button-based file picker — drag-and-drop is a convenience, never the only way to upload."},"613":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-30","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Replace the default text with `children` to communicate the accepted file types and size limits up front."},"614":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-31","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Let the drop zone fill its container; constrain it with the surrounding layout rather than setting a fixed width on the component itself."},"615":{"id":"/docs/components/drop-zone-32","page_id":"/docs/components/drop-zone","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/drop-zone#best-practices","content":"Reflect upload state (validating, uploading, error) outside the drop zone so the target area stays clear and predictable."},"616":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"page","content":"FieldError","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error"},"617":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-0","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-error","content":"Validation message for a field. Renders only when the field is invalid."},"618":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-1","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#features","content":"Features"},"619":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-2","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#installation","content":"Installation"},"620":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-3","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#examples","content":"Examples"},"621":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-4","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#default","content":"Default"},"622":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-5","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#props","content":"Props"},"623":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-6","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-error#fielderror","content":"FieldError"},"624":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-7","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-error#features","content":"Shown when the parent field is invalid (`isInvalid` or native constraint validation)."},"625":{"id":"/docs/components/field-error-8","page_id":"/docs/components/field-error","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-error#default","content":"FieldError renders when the field is invalid."},"626":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"page","content":"FileTrigger","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger"},"627":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-0","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger","content":"A style-less primitive that wraps any pressable component and opens the native file picker when it is activated."},"628":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-1","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Features"},"629":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-2","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#installation","content":"Installation"},"630":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-3","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#examples","content":"Examples"},"631":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-4","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#default","content":"Default"},"632":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-5","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accepted-types","content":"Accepted Types"},"633":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-6","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"634":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-7","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"635":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-8","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#props","content":"Props"},"636":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-9","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#filetrigger","content":"FileTrigger"},"637":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-10","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Turns any pressable component (such as an Antares `Button`) into a file picker trigger."},"638":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-11","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Renders a visually hidden `<input type=\"file\">` — no styling of its own."},"639":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-12","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Restricts selection by MIME type, allows multiple files, directory selection, and camera capture."},"640":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-13","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#features","content":"Resets the input value before every open, so re-selecting the same file still fires `onSelect`."},"641":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-14","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#default","content":"Wrap any pressable component. Activating the child opens the native file picker; the selected files arrive in `onSelect`."},"642":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-15","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accepted-types","content":"Restrict the picker to specific MIME types with `acceptedFileTypes`, and allow more than one file with `allowsMultiple`."},"643":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-16","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#accessibility","content":"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."},"644":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-17","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."},"645":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-18","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Pair `FileTrigger` with `DropZone` to offer both click-to-browse and drag-and-drop. See the DropZone \"File Upload\" example."},"646":{"id":"/docs/components/file-trigger-19","page_id":"/docs/components/file-trigger","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/file-trigger#best-practices","content":"Keep the child a single pressable element; `FileTrigger` forwards press behavior to whatever you nest inside it."},"647":{"id":"/docs/components/image","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"page","content":"Image","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image"},"648":{"id":"/docs/components/image-0","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image","content":"A native image element that inherits presentation and behavior from its Antares parent."},"649":{"id":"/docs/components/image-1","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#features","content":"Features"},"650":{"id":"/docs/components/image-2","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#installation","content":"Installation"},"651":{"id":"/docs/components/image-3","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#examples","content":"Examples"},"652":{"id":"/docs/components/image-4","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#default","content":"Default"},"653":{"id":"/docs/components/image-5","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"654":{"id":"/docs/components/image-6","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#props","content":"Props"},"655":{"id":"/docs/components/image-7","page_id":"/docs/components/image","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image#image","content":"Image"},"656":{"id":"/docs/components/image-8","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#features","content":"Renders a native `<img>` and accepts all of its attributes"},"657":{"id":"/docs/components/image-9","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#features","content":"Inherits presentation and behavior when composed inside Antares components such as Avatar"},"658":{"id":"/docs/components/image-10","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#features","content":"Ships no default styles, loading state, or fallback so it stays predictable everywhere"},"659":{"id":"/docs/components/image-11","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#default","content":"Render an image with alternative text and explicit dimensions."},"660":{"id":"/docs/components/image-12","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#accessibility","content":"Provide concise, meaningful `alt` text when the image conveys information."},"661":{"id":"/docs/components/image-13","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#accessibility","content":"Use `alt=\"\"` for decorative images or images already described by adjacent text."},"662":{"id":"/docs/components/image-14","page_id":"/docs/components/image","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image#accessibility","content":"Set `width` and `height` when known to reserve space and reduce layout shift."},"663":{"id":"/docs/components/heading","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"page","content":"Heading","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading"},"664":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-0","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading","content":"Semantic h1-h6 heading. Use slot=\"title\" inside a Modal or Dialog to name the overlay."},"665":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-1","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"Features"},"666":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-2","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#installation","content":"Installation"},"667":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-3","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#examples","content":"Examples"},"668":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-4","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#default","content":"Default"},"669":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-5","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"670":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-6","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#props","content":"Props"},"671":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-7","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/heading#heading","content":"Heading"},"672":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-8","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"Renders `h1`-`h6` from the `level` prop (default `3`). The level never changes the visual size."},"673":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-9","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"Without `size`, takes the heading tier of the surrounding `SizeProvider`.\n`size` picks a step on the heading ramp (`xs` to `2xl`)."},"674":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-10","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."},"675":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-11","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#features","content":"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."},"676":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-12","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#default","content":"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."},"677":{"id":"/docs/components/heading-13","page_id":"/docs/components/heading","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/heading#sizes","content":"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."},"678":{"id":"/docs/components/input","page_id":"/docs/components/input","type":"page","content":"Input","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/input"},"679":{"id":"/docs/components/input-0","page_id":"/docs/components/input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/input","content":"Single-line text control for use inside a field."},"680":{"id":"/docs/components/input-1","page_id":"/docs/components/input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/input#installation","content":"Installation"},"681":