oup container"],[1366,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[444,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1140,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[339,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1241,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[442,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1138,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1137,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[441,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1139,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[443,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2097,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[490,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[205,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[255,"`CardGroup` uses grid navigation: Tab enters or leaves, arrow keys move between Cards, and Space\nchanges selection. Enter activates row actions or links. Choose selection or `onAction`;\ncombining them prevents pointer selection."],[1908,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[324,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[394,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[412,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[390,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[405,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1845,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[481,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[491,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[492,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[483,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[2065,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1174,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[811,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[814,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[810,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[812,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[813,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[815,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1501,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[530,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1651,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[564,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[674,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1642,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1650,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1084,"`Enter/Space`"],[60,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[488,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[606,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[726,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[573,"`Escape`"],[989,"`Escape`"],[1086,"`Escape`"],[1850,"`Escape`"],[643,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2134,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[819,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2172,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[676,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[495,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[714,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[685,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[2048,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[677,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2103,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[878,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2102,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[913,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[203,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[533,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[982,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[977,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1173,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1900,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run down the side and values across the bottom. Reach for it when the labels are long or the chart is really a ranking."],[1610,"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."],[1840,"`overlay` elevation panel positioned relative to its trigger, with an optional arrow"],[1058,"`PaginationDots` is decorative and does not replace interactive page\ncontrols."],[734,"`placement` does not flip in RTL; the side is decided by document/flex order."],[717,"`placement` selects the collapse axis (`left`/`right` → width, `top`/`bottom` → height)"],[1078,"`PopoverTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Popover>`, handling open state and positioning automatically.\nBased on RAC `DialogTrigger`. To anchor a popover to an element it doesn't wrap, pass `triggerRef` instead."],[720,"`prefers-reduced-motion` support"],[1112,"`Pressable` accepts the React Aria press props, including `onPress`, `onPressStart`, `onPressEnd`, `onPressUp`, and `onPressChange`."],[1117,"`Pressable` automatically applies React Aria state attributes such as `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`, `[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` to the child. Ensure the child component styles these states appropriately if it overrides the default `Pressable` styles."],[1228,"`RadioGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Radio` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Radio` takes label text next to the indicator. `orientation` also sets keyboard-navigation direction and ARIA."],[2067,"`renderTooltip` example combining a pair of series. Each pair shares a `colorIndex`\n(solid actual + dashed forecast); hovering either line shows the percent change of\nthe forecast against the actual for that pair, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[2068,"`renderTooltip` example styled as a period-over-period comparison card. Paired series\n(solid current period + dashed previous period) share a `colorIndex`; hovering either\nline shows both dated values and the percent change, wrapped in the default popover."],[2066,"`renderTooltip` lets you render a fully custom tooltip and know which curve is\nhovered. Paired series share a `colorIndex`; hovering either line shows a\ntooltip specific to that line, wrapped in the default styled popover."],[991,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[1088,"`role=\"dialog\"` is applied automatically by the underlying React Aria `Dialog`"],[577,"`role=\"dialog\"` with `aria-modal=\"true\"` on the drawer panel (via RAC Modal)"],[818,"`role=\"img\"`: When title prop is provided"],[817,"`role=\"presentation\"`: For decorative icons"],[440,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1136,"`role=\"progressbar\"` on the container"],[1238,"`role=\"radio\"` on each option"],[1363,"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"],[1237,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1362,"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"],[1802,"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` → `role=\"toolbar\"` on container, `role=\"button\"` + `aria-pressed` per item"],[1801,"`selectionMode=\"single\"` → `role=\"radiogroup\"` on container, `role=\"radio\"` + `aria-checked` per item"],[919,"`size` controls item density. Shown here as two standalone menus so both\nsizes are visible at once; in practice you set `size` on the `Menu` inside a\n`MenuTrigger`."],[1641,"`size` picks a step on the component's own ramp (`xs` to `2xl`) and changes only the font size."],[1719,"`size` sets every part, each on its own role ramp. Without it, the lockup follows the size\nscope."],[1025,"`size` sets the label, input, and steppers. Without it, the field follows the surrounding size\nscope."],[1691,"`size` sets the label, input, description, and any control composed inside. Without it, the\nfield follows the surrounding size scope."],[545,"`size` sets the label, trigger, and calendar. Without it, the picker follows the surrounding\nsize scope."],[983,"`size` sets the modal's text, controls, and spacing. Without it, the modal follows the size\nscope around its trigger."],[675,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name, and takes the overlay's\ntitle tier, one step above the heading tier."],[2101,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[1419,"`sm`, `md`, or `lg` for the adopted components inside (listed below): their text, controls, and\ndefault spacing."],[95,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1527,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[1175,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[93,"`Tab`"],[575,"`Tab`"],[604,"`Tab`"],[728,"`Tab`"],[987,"`Tab`"],[1848,"`Tab`"],[58,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[486,"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"],[1614,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1611,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1615,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force