ain` pin down exactly which categories and value range to draw. Here category `F` has no data and still gets an empty slot, and the Y range stays `[0, 40]` even though the largest bar is 30 - handy when several charts need to share a scale."],[2052,"`xDomain` and `yDomain` pin the visible range. Use them to keep a fixed scale, or to keep several charts comparable."],[2043,"`xGridlines` and `yGridlines` add faint lines across the plot so it is easier to read a value back off an axis."],[2104,"`xl` - Extra large spacing"],[2045,"`xLabels` and `yLabels` toggle the tick labels on each axis. Turn them off for sparklines or when the surrounding UI already names the values."],[2053,"`xNice` and `yNice` round the domain out to friendlier numbers (e.g. 0.2 to 1.0), so ticks land on values people expect."],[2056,"`xPaddingOuter` and `yPaddingOuter` add breathing room at the ends of a band or point scale so the first and last values are not pinned to the edges."],[2100,"`xs` - Extra small spacing"],[1903,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - abbreviated dates on one axis, thousands separators on the other. The functions receive the raw accessor value, so they also cover currency, units, or percentages."],[2049,"`xTickFormat` and `yTickFormat` shape the axis labels - dates, currency, units, percentages - and the tooltip follows the same formatting."],[2046,"`xTickMarks` and `yTickMarks` draw the short lines at each tick value, which helps tie a label to its exact position on the axis."],[2044,"`xTitle` and `yTitle` label what each axis actually measures, e.g. \"Month\" and \"Temperature (°F)\"."],[2054,"`xZero` and `yZero` stretch the domain to include zero. Worth doing when the absolute size of the values matters, not just their movement."],[1939,"✅ Custom domains"],[1940,"✅ Design system alignment"],[1532,"✅ For binary on/off preferences (e.g. Wi-Fi, notifications, dark mode)"],[1806,"✅ For compact action grouping — related actions in space-constrained layouts (e.g. Undo / Redo, Zoom In / Out / Reset)"],[1805,"✅ For grouped contextual actions — two or more closely related actions that belong together (e.g. Bold / Italic / Underline, Align Left / Center / Right)"],[1807,"✅ For multi-select scenarios — when users need to select multiple options simultaneously"],[343,"✅ For selecting multiple independent options"],[1531,"✅ For settings that take effect immediately, without a form submission"],[345,"✅ For toggling settings or features on/off"],[1938,"✅ Interactive tooltips"],[1937,"✅ Responsive behavior with sticky axes"],[1935,"✅ Single and multi-series support"],[1936,"✅ Vertical and horizontal orientations"],[346,"✅ When all available options should be visible"],[1244,"✅ When all options should be visible at once"],[1245,"✅ When the decision is important and deserves space"],[1243,"✅ When there are 2-7 mutually exclusive options"],[344,"✅ When users can select zero, one, or many items"],[1247,"❌ For binary yes/no choices (use Checkbox or Toggle instead)"],[1534,"❌ For choosing one of several mutually exclusive options (use `Radio` or `SegmentedController` instead)"],[1809,"❌ For more than 5 choices — cognitive overload; consider a **Select** instead"],[1246,"❌ For more than 7 options (use Select instead)"],[1812,"❌ For mutually exclusive content views (e.g. Monthly / Yearly) — use **SegmentedController** instead"],[347,"❌ For mutually exclusive options (use Radio instead)"],[1533,"❌ For selections that require a \"Save\" or \"Submit\" action (use `Checkbox` instead)"],[348,"❌ For simple on/off toggles without labels (use Toggle/Switch instead)"],[1808,"❌ For unrelated actions that perform disconnected tasks without shared context"],[1810,"❌ When actions require strong visual distinction (e.g. Save vs. Delete)"],[1811,"❌ When selecting an option leads to a different page or workflow — use navigation instead"],[1248,"❌ When space is limited (use Select dropdown)"],[1943,"🚧 Additional customization options (tick formattin